+// True for a drawable caster. Structural, matching prepareScene3DRender's own mesh test: the test is a
+// predicate rather than an assertion so the traversal keeps the owner it already holds. The emitter
+// flattens interface heritage into independent owners, so `node as unknown as Mesh` asks C++ for a cast
+// between two unrelated owners that no runtime check backs; the predicate costs the same read and keeps
+// the original owner, which is what the rest of the pass consumes.
+function isShadowMesh(node: NodeOf<Node3DTraits>): node is Mesh {
+  const candidate: { readonly geometry?: MeshGeometry | null } = node;
+  return candidate.geometry != null;
+}
